    "body": "Hmm... i wanted my iframe to be sandboxed and having javascript disabled. \r\nhowever i would still like to be able to control it myself using javascript & allow-same-origin\r\n\r\nunfortunately when javascript is disabled (with not having allow-scripts) \r\nthen i can't paint anything inside of an iframe with scripts disabled that has a canvas element.\r\n\r\n> if [scripting is disabled](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-n-noscript) for the canvas element or if support for canvas elements has been disabled, the canvas element [represents](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#represents) its [fallback content](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#fallback-content) instead.\r\n\r\n\r\nrelated: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/76067397/canvas-drawing-in-a-sandboxed-iframe",
